      "claim_id": "c7",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "reasoning": "Passage [4] states the effective maximum for `vacuum_freeze_table_age` is $0.95 \\times \\text{autovacuum\\_freeze\\_max\\_age}$. Passage [5] states the default `autovacuum_freeze_max_age` is 200 million. $0.95 \\times 200 \\text{ million} = 190 \\text{ million}$. The claim says 180 million. Wait. $0.95 \\times 200 = 190$. The claim says 180. This is a contradiction if we assume strict math. Or is it unsupported? Let's re-read carefully. Passage [4]: 'The effective maximum for vacuum_freeze_table_age is 0.95 * autovacuum_freeze_max_age'. If default is 200M (Passage [5]), max is 190M. Claim says 180M. 180 != 190. So it is CONTRADICTED.",
      "citations": [
