          "index": 4,
          "quote": "The effective maximum for vacuum_freeze_table_age is 0.95 * autovacuum_freeze_max_age"
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "quote": "The default, 200 million transactions"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c8",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "reasoning": "Passage [6] states warnings start when oldest XIDs are 40 million from wraparound. Passage [7] states new XIDs are refused when fewer than 3 million are left. The difference is $40 - 3 = 37$ million.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 6,
          "quote": "when the database's oldest XIDs reach forty million transactions from the wraparound point"
        },
        {
          "index": 7,
          "quote": "once there are fewer than three million transactions left until wraparound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c9",
      "verdict": "CONTRADICTED",
      "reasoning": "Passage [8] explicitly states that once XID assignment stops (refuses to assign new XIDs), read-only transactions can still be started.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 8,
          "quote": "In this condition any transactions already in progress can continue, but only read-only transactions can be started."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
